# The quickstart's own build output. `go build -o openrealtime ./cmd/openrealtime`
# is the first command in the README, so every reader ends up with a fifty-
# megabyte binary here; leaving it untracked-but-listed makes `git status` lie
# about whether the tree is clean.
/openrealtime

# The official-SDK example installs its client from npm and builds a browser
# bundle from it. Neither is ours to vendor: the point of that example is that
# the client is the published package rather than a copy of it.
examples/sdk-client/node_modules/
examples/sdk-client/dist/
